# Goal 13: Fix `logb` subnormal exponent

## Function
`logb` (double-precision extract exponent)

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/logbd.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s6/src/mathd.rs` (around line 3103, `logbd`)

## Problem
MISMATCH — 2 test failures. Off-by-one for subnormal inputs (same pattern as `ilogb` Bug B).

```
C:    logb 0x1p-1074 = -0x1.0c8p+10   (= -1074.0)
Rust: logb 0x1p-1074 = -0x1.0ccp+10   (= -1075.0)

C:    logb 0x1p-1073 = -0x1.0c4p+10   (= -1073.0)
Rust: logb 0x1p-1073 = -0x1.0c8p+10   (= -1074.0)
```

Subnormal exponents are consistently 1 too low.

## What Needs to Change
Fix the subnormal normalization in `logbd`. The leading-zero count or the bias subtraction after normalization is off by one. Compare against the C implementation's subnormal handling path.

## Success Criteria
- `logb(0x1p-1074)` = `-0x1.0c8p+10` (= -1074.0, bitwise match)
- `logb(0x1p-1073)` = `-0x1.0c4p+10` (= -1073.0, bitwise match)
- All other `logb` tests continue to pass
